# Downstream REST Error Mapping — TokenRealty

Human doc: [docs/rules/rest-client-errors.md](../../docs/rules/rest-client-errors.md).

## Shared infrastructure (`tokenrealty-web/rest`)

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| `RestHeaders` | `X-Trace-Id`, MDC key, `Idempotency-Key` |
| `RestClientOperations` | Raw GET/POST/PATCH/PUT + header helpers |
| `DownstreamServices` | `ServiceSpec` constants (PAYMENT, COMPLIANCE, …) |
| `DownstreamClientErrors` | 5xx/timeout → `ValidationException`; 404 → `ResourceNotFoundException` |
| `DownstreamRestClientSupport` | Base class for outbound adapters |

Build `RestClient` beans with `ServiceRestClientBuilder` (`tokenrealty-security`) — Bearer token, timeout, `X-Trace-Id` from MDC.

## Required: use `RestClientOperations`

**Never** call `restClient.get().uri(...).retrieve()` (or post/patch/put) directly in `*Client` classes.

| Layer | Allowed API |
|-------|-------------|
| `*ClientConfig` | `ServiceRestClientBuilder.build(...)` → raw `RestClient` `@Bean` only |
| `*Client` | Extend `DownstreamRestClientSupport` → `get` / `post` / `patchVoid` / … |
| Rare custom URI | `http()` on the base class → `RestClientOperations` (still no raw `RestClient`) |

`DownstreamRestClientSupport` delegates transport to `RestClientOperations` and errors to `DownstreamClientErrors`. Do not bypass either layer.

Headers: use `RestClientOperations.idempotencyKey(...)` and `RestClientOperations.header(...)` — not manual `.header()` chains on raw `RestClient`.

## Required mapping

| Condition | Exception |
|-----------|-----------|
| 5xx or timeout (`ResourceAccessException`) | `ValidationException` — `{service} unavailable` |
| 404 on resource lookup (when `notFoundMessage` set) | `ResourceNotFoundException` |
| Other 4xx | `ValidationException` — `{service} rejected request: {detail}` |

Do not catch domain exceptions in client adapters. Extend `DownstreamRestClientSupport` instead of duplicating try/catch.

## Pattern

```java
@Component
public class PaymentClient extends DownstreamRestClientSupport {

    public PaymentClient(@Qualifier("paymentRestClient") RestClient restClient) {
        super(restClient);
    }

    public InitiatePaymentResponse initiateTokenPurchase(UUID orderId, ...) {
        return post("/v1/payments", body, InitiatePaymentResponse.class,
                DownstreamServices.PAYMENT,
                RestClientOperations.idempotencyKey("marketplace-order-" + orderId));
    }
}
```

`*ClientConfig` — one `@Bean` per base URL with explicit timeout:

```java
return ServiceRestClientBuilder.build(baseUrl, Duration.ofSeconds(10), serviceTokenProvider);
```

## Rules

* **Use `RestClientOperations` via `DownstreamRestClientSupport`** — no direct `RestClient` calls in client adapters
* No silent failures — no empty `catch (Exception)` that returns null (use `getAllowNull` when 404 is valid)
* Propagate `Authorization` via `ServiceTokenProvider`; propagate `X-Trace-Id` via builder interceptor
* Retries: only for idempotent GET; never auto-retry POST without idempotency key
* Migrate remaining `*Client` classes incrementally — reference: `PaymentClient`, `ComplianceClient`

